WEBVTT

00:08.920 --> 00:12.210
This is hilarious! I won all by myself!

00:12.210 --> 00:16.280
I'm actually the last one on this island!

00:23.090 --> 00:24.980
<i>They've formed a line?</i>

00:24.980 --> 00:28.430
<i>And they've all taken on the 
same stone pose for some reason.</i>

00:45.370 --> 00:46.970
Footsteps?

00:56.340 --> 00:59.450
Was that sound...

01:06.290 --> 01:08.880
<i>No! It's not a living creature!</i>

01:08.880 --> 01:11.090
<i>Is it their sorcery?</i>

01:13.770 --> 01:16.430
<i>Five meters. One second.</i>

01:25.050 --> 01:28.400
Damn, did Ukyo get it wrong?

01:28.400 --> 01:32.650
Nah, I guess it doesn't work 
unless you talk at it up close.

01:34.730 --> 01:36.620
Yo, Ibara.

01:38.230 --> 01:40.990
Guess it's just the two of us.

01:40.990 --> 01:46.910
Time for our happy science versus 
Medusa one-on-one boss fight.

03:25.610 --> 03:29.750
H-How the hell are you alive?!

03:29.750 --> 03:34.960
I enveloped the entire island 
in the petrification beam!

03:36.330 --> 03:37.480
Why else?

03:37.480 --> 03:46.580
It's so I can have that precious, almighty 
petrification weapon of yours there.

03:48.960 --> 03:54.040
That man, Oarashi, has the Medusa!

03:54.270 --> 03:56.090
He's going to engulf the island!

03:56.310 --> 03:57.930
Stop him!

03:58.520 --> 04:00.970
<i>Think! How do I avoid it?</i>

04:00.970 --> 04:03.440
<i>Get outside the petrification beam's range?</i>

04:03.440 --> 04:05.230
<i>I'll never make it in time.</i>

04:05.230 --> 04:08.930
<i>Then maybe I stick my finger in 
the revival fluid pre-preemptively?</i>

04:08.930 --> 04:16.250
<i>Would it actually undo the petrification 
exactly one beat after it hits?</i>

04:16.250 --> 04:19.860
<i>Or would it stave off the petrification?</i>

04:19.860 --> 04:24.010
<i>As long as I can't experiment, 
I have no way to know for sure.</i>

04:24.010 --> 04:25.700
<i>If it's the latter...</i>

04:26.090 --> 04:30.700
<i>The finger that's spared from petrification 
will rot off, and that's it.</i>

04:31.240 --> 04:33.180
<i>Which means the only move I have is...</i>

04:33.590 --> 04:34.650
Senku!

04:35.600 --> 04:41.020
The petrification beam always 
grows at the same speed!

04:44.920 --> 04:46.740
Looks like you've come up with something.

04:46.740 --> 04:49.750
Sure did! I've got the sickest, 
most disgusting plan.

04:52.280 --> 04:53.720
We all line up.

04:53.720 --> 04:55.850
All the exact same distance apart!

04:58.770 --> 05:01.750
He doesn't have anything!

05:01.750 --> 05:03.050
Why?!

05:03.050 --> 05:09.410
Ibara-sama told me that I won't be 
petrified if I go to the middle of the island!

05:11.960 --> 05:14.130
This can't be!

05:22.180 --> 05:23.710
Let's call it...

05:23.710 --> 05:25.130
the width of the lab car!

05:26.540 --> 05:27.950
<i>The lab car...</i>

05:27.950 --> 05:29.470
<i>Five meters!</i>

05:29.820 --> 05:33.100
Everyone, line up at the same distance 
as the person in front of you!

05:33.100 --> 05:35.860
Draw your hand out toward the light!

05:35.860 --> 05:39.520
Once your fingertips start petrifying, 
signal with your other hand!

05:40.010 --> 05:42.320
The signals will go up at the same rate.

05:42.320 --> 05:46.100
Senku will know how to measure its speed!

05:46.100 --> 05:50.180
He'll know the exact moment 
the light reaches him!

05:59.540 --> 06:01.790
Roughly 0.5 seconds for five meters.

06:01.790 --> 06:04.640
Which puts the wind speed... 
rather, the light's speed,

06:04.640 --> 06:06.920
at roughly 40 kilometers per hour.

06:07.240 --> 06:08.570
Oh, man!

06:08.570 --> 06:11.170
Let's go! 3,700 years since the last time!

06:11.170 --> 06:13.340
Yeah, I remember it was like this!

06:13.340 --> 06:15.930
You got this, Senku-chan!

06:17.700 --> 06:23.440
I know for sure that Senku's gonna 
make it out of the petrification!

06:23.760 --> 06:27.320
Sure, we're mere humans making these signals.

06:27.320 --> 06:33.010
But I bet you've got some crazy way 
of coming up with a precise number!

06:33.380 --> 06:36.530
Convey it as accurately as possible!

06:36.530 --> 06:40.080
That is the final task that we can take on!

06:41.930 --> 06:44.470
Let's beat the crap out of this damn beam!

06:44.470 --> 06:48.050
If we don't, I'll beat the crap out of you, Senku!

06:52.940 --> 06:57.170
<i>Using the method of least squares, 
the light's speed is 36 kilometers per hour.</i>

06:57.170 --> 06:59.690
<i>It'll reach me in about 5.5 seconds.</i>

06:59.690 --> 07:04.060
<i>I can buy time if I throw it high, 
but if I miss, we're screwed.</i>

07:04.060 --> 07:06.380
<i>I can maybe do three meters.</i>

07:06.380 --> 07:08.040
<i>Weight, 300 grams.</i>

07:08.040 --> 07:11.000
<i>Drag force, 0.21 kilograms per meter.</i>

07:11.000 --> 07:13.750
<i>With acceleration due to gravity 
9.8 meters per second squared...</i>

07:13.750 --> 07:16.740
<i>If I throw it up at a rate 
of 33 kilometers per hour,</i>

07:17.070 --> 07:19.670
<i>it'll reach 3 meters in 0.72 seconds.</i>

07:20.040 --> 07:22.580
<i>Once it's in free fall, it'll hit me in...</i>

07:22.580 --> 07:25.880
<b>1.8 seconds</b>

07:23.370 --> 07:25.330
<i>1.8 seconds.</i>

07:26.210 --> 07:29.770
<i>Basically, my job is to 
wait exactly four seconds,</i>

07:29.770 --> 07:33.090
<i>and then throw the revival fluid 
three meters into the air.</i>

07:33.540 --> 07:36.220
<i>Too early, and it'll hit 
me before I'm petrified.</i>

07:36.220 --> 07:39.020
<i>Too late, and I'll be 
stoned before I throw it.</i>

07:39.020 --> 07:41.010
<i>If it isn't perfect, I die.</i>

07:41.010 --> 07:45.270
<i>What I need is a ten billion 
percent perfect countdown.</i>

07:48.240 --> 07:51.360
<i>One, two, three...</i>

07:49.800 --> 07:56.370
<i>Sadly, I've had a ridiculous 
3,700 years of practice doing that.</i>

07:51.360 --> 07:56.370
<i>four, five, six, seven, eight..</i>

08:47.040 --> 08:48.730
<i>I knew it.</i>

08:50.300 --> 08:55.190
<i>The revival fluid prevented 
petrification from the start.</i>

08:56.410 --> 09:00.800
<i>It looks like you can avoid being petrified 
wherever your body's in the fluid.</i>

09:01.970 --> 09:04.820
<i>I might have been dead if I'd 
had just my finger in there.</i>

09:05.940 --> 09:09.850
<i>So then, if you're diving in revival fluid,</i>

09:09.850 --> 09:13.320
<i>the petrification beam goes right 
through you ten billion percent.</i>

09:14.460 --> 09:18.380
<i>Instead, you'll croak from 
being drenched in nitric acid.</i>

09:52.230 --> 09:54.820
<i>Shit! Ibara's already here!</i>

09:58.610 --> 10:02.330
<i>I'll set a Kingdom of Science specialty trap.</i>

10:18.830 --> 10:22.310
H-How the hell are you alive?!

10:22.310 --> 10:27.480
I enveloped the entire island 
in the petrification beam!

10:29.130 --> 10:32.010
I fancy myself a bit of a science user.

10:32.010 --> 10:35.730
Tempt me with an out-of-place high-tech 
artifact like a petrification beam,

10:35.730 --> 10:39.700
and I'm gonna be exhilarated 
ten billion percent.

10:41.160 --> 10:43.810
Oh, I forgot to mention...

10:43.810 --> 10:46.290
During that brief moment 
I was waiting for you,

10:46.510 --> 10:50.620
I crafted up some extreme, cutting-edge 
technology of the kind that

10:50.620 --> 10:54.630
Google and Toyota have been working 
their asses off to develop.

10:54.910 --> 10:58.760
It's the birth of the self-driving car!

10:58.380 --> 11:00.130
m 0 0 l 196 0 l 196 80 l 0 80

10:58.380 --> 11:00.130
Self-driving
AI acquired!!

11:10.230 --> 11:13.520
Although it's more of a 
Rube Goldberg machine!

11:13.230 --> 11:14.980
m 0 0 l 280 0 l 280 60 l 0 60

11:13.230 --> 11:14.980
Except it's a sham!

11:18.230 --> 11:23.460
Ah, right, you aren't a modern man, 
so of course you wouldn't know...

11:23.460 --> 11:26.700
You shouldn't be messing around near cars.

11:27.730 --> 11:32.710
<i>The Kingdom of Science's boss duel 
against the Petrification Kingdom</i>

11:33.010 --> 11:35.800
<i>is won by the one who gets the Medusa's eye!</i>

11:36.380 --> 11:37.650
And that's me!

11:39.940 --> 11:41.520
<i>Where is Ibara?</i>

11:41.520 --> 11:42.970
<i>Under the car?</i>

11:43.810 --> 11:45.890
Three meters, three—

11:57.770 --> 12:02.490
This old man here is <i>really</i> cautious.

12:02.960 --> 12:05.230
Of course I am!

12:05.230 --> 12:09.750
I even came prepared in case you 
might use projectiles against me!

12:11.190 --> 12:16.920
Although I didn't expect that sorcery attack.

12:17.170 --> 12:19.610
Well, sorcery user...

12:19.610 --> 12:25.770
How about we get started on that 
boss fight you've been asking for?

12:28.010 --> 12:30.860
The chief, fleeing from the get-go?

12:31.280 --> 12:33.560
You coward.

12:41.970 --> 12:43.950
<i>He must know that he has no way to avoid</i>

12:43.950 --> 12:47.070
<i>the petrification weapon once 
it's been thrown at him.</i>

12:47.340 --> 12:50.200
<i>I can't throw it here. It would 
get caught on the branches.</i>

12:50.810 --> 12:55.710
<i>Was he not being a coward, 
but luring me into the trees?</i>

13:00.270 --> 13:02.010
Sorcery...

13:03.130 --> 13:05.610
You weren't being a coward. It's a trap.

13:05.610 --> 13:07.970
Not bad!

13:08.190 --> 13:11.770
<i>Shit... I have nothing 
left to use as a weapon.</i>

13:12.470 --> 13:13.940
But there's one problem...

13:13.940 --> 13:18.480
No one knows this island's 
geography better than I do!

13:18.480 --> 13:20.590
Too bad for you!

13:20.590 --> 13:24.190
I'm the one setting the trap!

13:24.190 --> 13:26.330
I just need to pretend

13:26.330 --> 13:30.230
I'm being lured as I'm really just 
cornering you out in the open!

13:55.790 --> 13:58.520
This here is a sorcery weapon.

13:58.520 --> 14:01.450
You've already been shot in the hand 
with it. You know what it feels like.

14:01.450 --> 14:05.090
It's gonna pew-pew you with science arrows.

14:05.090 --> 14:07.200
Don't bother with that bluff.

14:07.200 --> 14:10.840
I've been watching you carefully.

14:10.840 --> 14:13.450
That's not what that tool does.

14:13.450 --> 14:16.870
If it was a projectile, you would 
have already shot it at me.

14:16.870 --> 14:21.810
But I'm also not enough of 
an idiot to go near sorcery.

14:21.810 --> 14:23.110
I told you.

14:23.110 --> 14:27.300
This old man here is <i>really</i> cautious.

14:27.850 --> 14:30.610
I'll give you an opportunity 
to tell me before your end.

14:30.950 --> 14:32.800
What's your name?

14:34.280 --> 14:38.560
<i>He's trying to buy time to 
estimate his distance to me.</i>

14:39.210 --> 14:41.050
Five meters.

14:41.050 --> 14:43.000
Five seconds.

14:44.600 --> 14:46.160
Senku.

14:46.160 --> 14:48.570
Ishigami Senku.

14:48.570 --> 14:50.290
Uh-huh.

14:50.290 --> 14:51.670
Hello.

14:51.670 --> 14:57.260
And goodbye forever, Senku-chan!

15:02.800 --> 15:04.650
<i>This whooshing sound...</i>

15:04.990 --> 15:06.300
<i>Isn't this...</i>

15:07.160 --> 15:09.600
<i>The cliff of the howling seas?</i>

15:16.120 --> 15:19.020
They've arrived at the 
cliff of the howling seas.

15:45.210 --> 15:49.460
My next transmission is my signal.

15:50.220 --> 15:53.190
I'll give you an opportunity 
to tell me before your end.

15:53.190 --> 15:54.840
What's your name?

15:55.450 --> 15:57.020
Senku.

15:57.020 --> 15:59.350
Ishigami Senku.

16:07.690 --> 16:09.940
What is that bird?!

16:11.660 --> 16:15.180
We have an actual boss fight now!

16:15.180 --> 16:20.040
Thanks for the Medusa. 
We're taking it in mid-air!

16:22.890 --> 16:25.080
I want everything in the world!

16:25.530 --> 16:29.920
The supertechnology device that is the Medusa

16:31.100 --> 16:36.050
using the culmination of the Kingdom 
of Science's ingenuity: the drone!

16:36.350 --> 16:37.470
Pull!

16:58.080 --> 17:02.740
I'm not going down to some damn youths, 
even if there are two of you!

17:02.740 --> 17:05.610
I used to be a warrior, after all!

17:11.840 --> 17:15.130
We aren't depending on brute strength here!

17:16.110 --> 17:18.820
Don't insult me! I know that!

17:18.820 --> 17:20.120
<i>That's right...</i>

17:20.120 --> 17:23.560
<i>I'm only pretending to be losing 
until the very last moment.</i>

17:23.900 --> 17:27.860
<i>Sadly for you, I'm a cautious man.</i>

17:27.860 --> 17:30.470
<i>This is a test of wit.</i>

17:30.470 --> 17:32.820
<i>They surely know that.</i>

17:33.060 --> 17:34.780
Now! Let go!

17:34.780 --> 17:37.320
Three. Two. One.

17:38.010 --> 17:40.320
I'm not messing up.

17:40.320 --> 17:42.580
Not at counting.

17:52.410 --> 17:54.390
Did you think this cautious old man

17:54.390 --> 17:59.820
wouldn't have practiced fighting 
off the petrification beam?

17:59.820 --> 18:05.600
I'd never mess up estimating its range.

18:05.600 --> 18:09.610
Here's some wisdom for the 
final moments of your lives!

18:09.610 --> 18:15.770
Those who think they're smart are 
the easiest ones to screw over!

18:15.770 --> 18:22.480
Did you brats really think you 
could be more sly than me?!

18:40.660 --> 18:43.920
Oh, my! Oh, my! This is what's 
wrong with idiots like you!

18:43.920 --> 18:48.640
Were you hoping to brute-force your 
way past the petrification beam?

18:51.230 --> 18:53.920
This thing is unavoidable!

18:53.920 --> 18:56.460
Goodbye for real this time!

18:56.460 --> 19:02.840
The last man standing in this 
long battle is this old man!

19:07.290 --> 19:11.620
You attached that thing that makes noise?

19:13.450 --> 19:15.130
Yeah, Ibara.

19:15.370 --> 19:17.590
You're exactly right.

19:17.970 --> 19:21.740
Those who think they're smart are 
the easiest ones to screw over.

19:23.210 --> 19:27.220
Five meters, one second.

19:30.360 --> 19:32.940
N-No!

19:32.940 --> 19:41.120
No!

20:16.940 --> 20:21.900
m 0 0 l 360 0 l 360 60 l 0 60

20:16.940 --> 20:21.900
Petrification device acquired!!

21:08.670 --> 21:09.880
I'm alone.

21:30.380 --> 21:31.420
Again.

21:34.000 --> 21:35.160
I'm alone again.

21:44.230 --> 21:46.480
<i>Can you hear me, Senku-san?</i>

21:48.200 --> 21:51.440
How are things over there, Senku-san?

21:55.850 --> 21:57.080
No.

22:09.930 --> 22:13.370
I'm not alone this time.

23:52.030 --> 23:54.990
<b>Next Episode</b>

23:54.990 --> 24:00.000
<b>This is a work of fiction, but the plants, 
animals, and production methods described are based on reality.
Foraging and making things on your own accord is extremely dangerous
and, in some cases, illegal. Please do not imitate without expertise.</b>
